{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"ff91daa7-3671-428b-aa4a-741e289da74b\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"According to NCERT, what principle was intended to guide relations between the Centre and the States in India?\",\"hi\":\"NCERT के अनुसार भारत में केंद्र और राज्यों के संबंधों का मार्गदर्शन किस सिद्धांत से होना था?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Permanent confrontation\",\"hi\":\"स्थायी टकराव\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Cooperation while recognising diversity and emphasising unity\",\"hi\":\"विविधता को मान्यता देते हुए और एकता पर बल देते हुए सहयोग\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Complete dependence of States on local bodies\",\"hi\":\"राज्यों की स्थानीय निकायों पर पूर्ण निर्भरता\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Separate international sovereignty for every State\",\"hi\":\"हर राज्य की अलग अंतरराष्ट्रीय संप्रभुता\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 7, Federalism, 2026-27 reprint, printed pp. 156, 158, 164 and 172. Direct official document: NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 7 (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps207.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ff33036c-979d-4033-b598-42e0370f5720\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"If difficulty arises in construing part of the Hindi translation under Article 394A, what does the Constitution require?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 394A के अधीन हिंदी अनुवाद के किसी भाग को समझने में कठिनाई उत्पन्न हो तो संविधान क्या अपेक्षा करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The translation automatically becomes void\",\"hi\":\"अनुवाद स्वतः शून्य हो जाता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The President must cause it to be suitably revised\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति उसका उपयुक्त पुनरीक्षण कराएँगे\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The Supreme Court must rewrite the entire Constitution\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय पूरे संविधान को पुनः लिखेगा\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Only Parliament may publish an unofficial summary\",\"hi\":\"केवल संसद अनौपचारिक सार प्रकाशित कर सकती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Article 394A(2)-(3) (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ff03fac8-d64e-4c99-9dc0-73c97cb83088\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which list consists entirely of liberties expressly named in the Preamble?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सी सूची पूरी तरह उन स्वतंत्रताओं से बनी है जिनका उद्देशिका में स्पष्ट उल्लेख है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Trade, movement, residence and profession\",\"hi\":\"व्यापार, संचरण, निवास और व्यवसाय\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Property, contract, inheritance and taxation\",\"hi\":\"संपत्ति, संविदा, उत्तराधिकार और कराधान\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Press, association, assembly and petition\",\"hi\":\"प्रेस, संगठन, सभा और याचिका\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Thought, expression, belief, faith and worship\",\"hi\":\"विचार, अभिव्यक्ति, विश्वास, धर्म और उपासना\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Preamble and Articles 19 and 25. Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fec9c247-e5b1-4e17-88d2-3a5733c1f7ae\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Consider the following statements about sovereignty: 1. India is free from external control. 2. Sovereignty allows every authority to ignore the Constitution. 3. The Constitution encourages respect for international law. Which are correct?\",\"hi\":\"प्रभुसत्ता के बारे में निम्न कथनों पर विचार कीजिए: 1. भारत बाहरी नियंत्रण से मुक्त है। 2. प्रभुसत्ता प्रत्येक प्राधिकारी को संविधान की उपेक्षा की अनुमति देती है। 3. संविधान अंतरराष्ट्रीय विधि के सम्मान को प्रोत्साहित करता है। कौन-से कथन सही हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"1 and 3 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1 और 3\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"1 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"2 and 3 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 2 और 3\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"1, 2 and 3\",\"hi\":\"1, 2 और 3\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 13-16, 19(1)(g), 25-30, 38-43, 47, 51, 51A(e), 253 and 325, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Sovereign, Socialist and Secular on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; constitutional philosophy, individual freedom, social justice, secularism and national identity\"},{\"title\":\"Senior Secondary Political Science (317), Lesson 5: Preamble and Salient Features\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS)\",\"url\":\"https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/317en/317EL5.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Lesson 5, sections 5.4-5.5; sovereignty discussion on printed p. 49\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"NIOS Political Science (317), Lesson 5, section 5.5; Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Articles 13 and 51(c)\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"febfe1c4-0b99-487a-bacb-0d0808a08473\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"The Union, State and Concurrent Lists are contained in which part of the constitutional scheme?\",\"hi\":\"संघ, राज्य और समवर्ती सूचियाँ संवैधानिक व्यवस्था के किस भाग में दी गई हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The Fifth Schedule alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल पाँचवीं अनुसूची\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The Seventh Schedule read with Article 246\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 246 के साथ पठित सातवीं अनुसूची\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The Tenth Schedule read with Article 102\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 102 के साथ पठित दसवीं अनुसूची\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The Preamble alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल प्रस्तावना\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 246, PDF p. 175, and Seventh Schedule, Lists I-III, PDF pp. 340-353. Direct official document: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fe6278f4-0108-4978-97ab-e3a2037bc847\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"According to the verified NCERT source table, Law-making procedure is associated with which source?\",\"hi\":\"सत्यापित NCERT स्रोत-सारणी के अनुसार विधि-निर्माण प्रक्रिया किस स्रोत से संबंधित है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Irish Constitution\",\"hi\":\"आयरिश संविधान\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"British Constitution\",\"hi\":\"ब्रिटिश संविधान\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"French Constitution\",\"hi\":\"फ्रांसीसी संविधान\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Canadian Constitution\",\"hi\":\"कनाडाई संविधान\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: NCERT Class XI, source table, printed p. 22; Constitution of India, relevant provisions. | Direct official documents: NCERT, Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 1 “Constitution: Why and How?”, Reprint 2026-27 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps201.pdf ; Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India, as on 1 May 2026 — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf | Verification date: 2026-07-13 | Confidence: high.\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fe403aa2-2a18-4256-b057-b6c53cd4c442\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What is the central idea of separation of powers in a constitutional government?\",\"hi\":\"संवैधानिक शासन में शक्तियों के पृथक्करण का केंद्रीय विचार क्या है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Legislative, executive and judicial functions are allocated to distinct organs under constitutional limits\",\"hi\":\"विधायी, कार्यकारी और न्यायिक कार्य संवैधानिक सीमाओं के अधीन अलग-अलग अंगों को सौंपे जाते हैं\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"All public power is permanently concentrated in one institution\",\"hi\":\"सभी सार्वजनिक शक्ति स्थायी रूप से एक संस्था में केंद्रित रहती है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Courts alone make, execute and interpret every law\",\"hi\":\"केवल न्यायालय हर कानून बनाते, लागू करते और उसकी व्याख्या करते हैं\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Political parties replace the constitutional organs of the State\",\"hi\":\"राजनीतिक दल राज्य के संवैधानिक अंगों का स्थान ले लेते हैं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Supreme Court of India, Divisional Manager, Aravali Golf Club v. Chander Hass, Civil Appeal No. 5732 of 2007, judgment dated 6 December 2007, paragraphs 19-24, official PDF pp. 3-5. Direct official document: Supreme Court of India, Divisional Manager, Aravali Golf Club v. Chander Hass (official PDF: https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/29995.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fdb6a549-c2ac-49a3-88da-672f36b14229\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 51’s call to respect international law and treaty obligations is best understood as:\",\"hi\":\"अंतरराष्ट्रीय विधि और संधि-बाध्यताओं के सम्मान के लिए अनुच्छेद 51 का आह्वान सबसे उपयुक्त रूप में कैसे समझा जाना चाहिए?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"A transfer of all sovereignty to foreign institutions\",\"hi\":\"सारी प्रभुसत्ता विदेशी संस्थाओं को हस्तांतरित करना\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"A prohibition on independent foreign policy\",\"hi\":\"स्वतंत्र विदेश नीति पर रोक\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A constitutional commitment compatible with India’s voluntary exercise of sovereignty\",\"hi\":\"भारत द्वारा प्रभुसत्ता के स्वैच्छिक प्रयोग के अनुकूल संवैधानिक प्रतिबद्धता\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A power of foreign courts to amend the Indian Constitution\",\"hi\":\"विदेशी न्यायालयों की भारतीय संविधान संशोधित करने की शक्ति\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot editio