35. Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"faf5a7c2-4d68-4cee-937e-50e97540f8c3\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A classification under Article 14 is ordinarily reasonable when it is based on:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 14 के अधीन वर्गीकरण सामान्यतः कब उचित माना जाता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Administrative convenience alone without any objective\",\"hi\":\"बिना उद्देश्य के केवल प्रशासनिक सुविधा\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"A distinction chosen secretly by an official\",\"hi\":\"किसी अधिकारी द्वारा गुप्त रूप से चुना गया भेद\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"An identical rule for every unequal situation\",\"hi\":\"हर असमान स्थिति के लिए बिल्कुल समान नियम\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"An intelligible differentia having a rational nexus with the statutory object\",\"hi\":\"कानून के उद्देश्य से तार्किक संबंध रखने वाला बोधगम्य अंतर\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Supreme Court of India, State of Tamil Nadu v. National South Indian River Interlinking Agriculturist Association, judgment dated 23 November 2021, paragraphs 14-15, official PDF pp. 9-10; Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 14. Direct official documents: Supreme Court of India, State of Tamil Nadu classification judgment (official PDF: https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2017/16734/16734_2017_4_1501_31612_Judgement_23-Nov-2021.pdf); Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fa9ada8a-8f7d-40fd-9e5f-5cfac731cf60\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which constitutional provisions most directly operationalise the secular ethos expressed by the Preamble?\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) द्वारा व्यक्त पंथनिरपेक्ष भाव को कौन-से संवैधानिक प्रावधान सबसे प्रत्यक्ष रूप से क्रियान्वित करते हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Articles 52-62 alone, dealing with the President\",\"hi\":\"केवल अनुच्छेद 52-62, जो राष्ट्रपति से संबंधित हैं\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Articles 14-16 on equality and non-discrimination, read with Articles 25-28 on religious freedom\",\"hi\":\"समता और भेदभाव-निषेध संबंधी अनुच्छेद 14-16 तथा धार्मिक स्वतंत्रता संबंधी अनुच्छेद 25-28\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Articles 123 and 213 on ordinances alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल अध्यादेशों से संबंधित अनुच्छेद 123 और 213\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The provisions on inter-State trade alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल अंतरराज्यीय व्यापार संबंधी प्रावधान\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified with: Constitution, Articles 14-16 and 25-28; Dr Balram Singh, para 3; Evidence locator: Articles 14-16 and 25-28; Balram paragraph 3, PDF pages 2-3; Direct clickable source(s): The Constitution of India, diglot edition: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf | Dr Balram Singh v. Union of India: https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2020/13773/13773_2020_1_39_57487_Judgement_25-Nov-2024.pdf; Confidence: high; Originality: independently written; no PYQ, textbook exercise, coaching question, or copyrighted explanation has been copied.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India, diglot edition\",\"institution\":\"Government of India, Legislative Department\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Dr Balram Singh v. Union of India\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2020/13773/13773_2020_1_39_57487_Judgement_25-Nov-2024.pdf\",\"citation\":\"2024 INSC 893\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Articles 14-16 and 25-28; Balram paragraph 3, PDF pages 2-3\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fa991b67-35e7-456d-be62-556b7f95ea74\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Assertion (A): A written Constitution can remain a “living document.”\\nReason (R): Its written text may be amended and interpreted while retaining an identifiable constitutional framework.\",\"hi\":\"अभिकथन (A): लिखित संविधान “जीवंत दस्तावेज” बना रह सकता है।\\nकारण (R): पहचान योग्य संवैधानिक ढाँचा बनाए रखते हुए उसके लिखित पाठ में संशोधन और उसकी व्याख्या की जा सकती है।\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A\",\"hi\":\"A और R दोनों सही हैं तथा R, A की सही व्याख्या है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A\",\"hi\":\"A और R दोनों सही हैं, किंतु R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A is true, but R is false\",\"hi\":\"A सही है, किंतु R गलत है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A is false, but R is true\",\"hi\":\"A गलत है, किंतु R सही है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 9, pp. 196-200 and 212-215 (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps209.pdf); Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Contents and amendment footnotes (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f92dc187-0595-4f42-a0b3-3f2c0edc8d1a\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Before Parliament can create a new All India Service under Article 312, Rajya Sabha must declare that it is necessary or expedient in the national interest by:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 312 के अधीन संसद नई अखिल भारतीय सेवा बनाए, उससे पहले राज्यसभा को राष्ट्रीय हित में इसकी आवश्यकता या समीचीनता किस बहुमत से घोषित करनी होती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Not less than two-thirds of members present and voting\",\"hi\":\"उपस्थित और मतदान करने वाले सदस्यों के कम-से-कम दो-तिहाई\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"A simple majority of Lok Sabha alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल लोकसभा का साधारण बहुमत\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Unanimous consent of all State Legislatures\",\"hi\":\"सभी राज्य विधानमंडलों की सर्वसम्मति\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A majority of the Supreme Court judges\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीशों का बहुमत\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 312(1)-(2), PDF p. 205. Direct official document: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f91a0fa7-9a27-48e4-826f-4cddfa689cd3\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which description best captures the constitutional design of Indian federalism?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सा वर्णन भारतीय संघवाद की संवैधानिक रचना को सबसे अच्छी तरह व्यक्त करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Independent sovereign States joined only by treaty\",\"hi\":\"केवल संधि से जुड़े स्वतंत्र संप्रभु राज्य\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"A wholly unitary system with no constitutional State sphere\",\"hi\":\"राज्यों के संवैधानिक क्षेत्र के बिना पूर्ण एकात्मक व्यवस्था\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A confederation whose central authority depends on State permission\",\"hi\":\"ऐसा परिसंघ जिसकी केंद्रीय सत्ता राज्य अनुमति पर निर्भर है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A federal division of powers combined with significant Union-strengthening provisions\",\"hi\":\"शक्तियों का संघीय विभाजन तथा संघ को मजबूत करने वाले महत्त्वपूर्ण प्रावधान\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 7, Federalism, 2026-27 reprint, printed pp. 158-163; Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Articles 3, 246, 248 and 353, PDF pp. 32-33, 175-176 and 240-241. Direct official documents: NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 7 (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps207.pdf); Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f8ffc9ad-b9c5-45f3-a05c-84e677095497\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"If the President asks the Council of Ministers to reconsider its advice under Article 74, what follows after reconsideration?\",\"hi\":\"यदि राष्ट्रपति अनुच्छेद 74 के अधीन मंत्रिपरिषद को अपनी सलाह पर पुनर्विचार करने को कहें, तो पुनर्विचार के बाद क्या होता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The President may reject the advice permanently\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति सलाह को स्थायी रूप से अस्वीकार कर सकते हैं\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The Supreme Court chooses the final policy\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय अंतिम नीति चुनता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A referendum becomes compulsory\",\"hi\":\"जनमत-संग्रह अनिवार्य हो जाता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The President must act according to the advice tendered after reconsideration\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति को पुनर्विचार के बाद दी गई सलाह के अनुसार कार्य करना होता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), proviso to Article 74(1), PDF p. 64. NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 4, Executive, 2026-27 reprint, printed pp. 88-89. Direct official documents: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf); NCERT Class 11, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 4 Executive (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps204.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f8c60dfb-f70b-4250-becb-1c3557200ef1\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which body was the formal maker of the Constitution of India?\",\"hi\":\"भारत के संविधान का औपचारिक निर्माता कौन-सा निकाय था?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Drafting Committee acting alone\",\"hi\":\"अकेले कार्यरत प्रारूप समिति\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"British Parliament\",\"hi\":\"ब्रिटिश संसद\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Constituent Assembly\",\"hi\":\"संविधान सभा\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Federal Court of India\",\"hi\":\"भारत का संघीय न्यायालय\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: NCERT Class IX, printed p. 24; Constitution, commencement note. | Direct official documents: NCERT, Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2 “Constitutional Design”, Reprint 2025-26 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf ; NCERT, Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 1 “Constitution: Why and How?”, Reprint 2026-27 — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps201.pdf ; Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India, as on 1 May 2026 — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf | Verification date: 2026-07-13 | Confidence: high.\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f878f0d9-962f-40f4-b642-42982da329fa\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which inference about 'Democratic' in the Preamble follows from Kihoto Hollohan v. Zachillhu?\",\"hi\":\"किहोटो होलोहन बनाम ज़ाचिल्हू से उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) के 'लोकतंत्रात्मक' शब्द के संबंध में कौन-सा निष्कर्ष निकलता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Election disputes should be decided by the political majority alone\",\"hi\":\"चुनावी विवादों का अंतिम निर्णय केवल राजनीतिक बहुमत करे\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Free and fair elections are optional conventions\",\"hi\":\"स्वतंत्र और निष्पक्ष चुनाव वैकल्पिक परंपराएँ हैं\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Democracy is part of the basic structure, and free and fair elections with independent dispute resolution are essential democratic features\",\"hi\":\"लोकतंत्र मूल संरचना का भाग है और स्वतंत्र विवाद-निपटान सहित स्वतंत्र एवं निष्पक्ष चुनाव आवश्यक लोकतांत्रिक विशेषताएँ हैं\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Judicial review is incompatible with parliamentary democracy\",\"hi\":\"न्यायिक पुनरावलोकन संसदीय लोकतंत्र से असंगत है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified with: Kihoto Hollohan, headnote 8.1 and majority discussion, PDF pp. 15-16, 83; Evidence locator: headnote 8.1, PDF pages 15-16; majority discussion, PDF page 83; Direct clickable source(s): Kihoto Hollohan v. Zachillhu: https://api.sci.gov.in/judgment/judis/12491.pdf; Confidence: high; Originality: independently written; no PYQ, textbook exercise, coaching question, or copyrighted explanation has been copied.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Kihoto Hollohan v. Zachillhu\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/judgment/judis/12491.pdf\",\"citation\":\"1992 Supp (2) SCC 651\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"headnote 8.1, PDF pages 15-16; majority discussion, PDF page 83\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},