 Salient Features\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS)\",\"url\":\"https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/317en/317EL5.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Lesson 5, sections 5.4-5.5; sovereignty discussion on printed p. 49\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"NIOS Political Science (317), Lesson 5, section 5.5, p. 49; Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Preamble and Articles 13 and 245\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f675ed9a-6cc0-4500-8a20-bc3b1980747a\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Does Parliament's amending power under Article 368 extend to the Preamble?\",\"hi\":\"क्या अनुच्छेद 368 के अधीन संसद की संशोधन शक्ति उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) तक विस्तृत है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"No, because the Preamble is outside the Constitution\",\"hi\":\"नहीं, क्योंकि उद्देशिका संविधान से बाहर है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Only after a national referendum\",\"hi\":\"केवल राष्ट्रीय जनमत-संग्रह के बाद\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Only with unanimous approval of all States\",\"hi\":\"केवल सभी राज्यों की सर्वसम्मत स्वीकृति से\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Yes, subject to the limitations governing constitutional amendments\",\"hi\":\"हाँ, संवैधानिक संशोधनों पर लागू सीमाओं के अधीन\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"Dr Balram Singh para 2\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Dr Balram Singh and Others v. Union of India and Another\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2020/13773/13773_2020_1_39_57487_Judgement_25-Nov-2024.pdf\",\"citation\":\"2024 INSC 835\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"para 2, judgment printed p.2 / PDF p.2\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f5a8969b-a382-4a8b-bb49-accfd84ecbeb\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Under Article 25(1), freedom of conscience and religion is expressly subject to:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 25(1) के अधीन अंतःकरण और धर्म की स्वतंत्रता स्पष्ट रूप से किनके अधीन है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Only the wishes of a local official\",\"hi\":\"केवल स्थानीय अधिकारी की इच्छा\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Public order, morality, health and the other provisions of Part III\",\"hi\":\"लोक व्यवस्था, सदाचार, स्वास्थ्य और भाग III के अन्य प्रावधान\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A compulsory State religion\",\"hi\":\"अनिवार्य राज्य-धर्म\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Approval by every religious denomination\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक धार्मिक संप्रदाय की स्वीकृति\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 13-16, 19(1)(g), 25-30, 38-43, 47, 51, 51A(e), 253 and 325, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Sovereign, Socialist and Secular on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; constitutional philosophy, individual freedom, social justice, secularism and national identity\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Article 25(1), PDF p. 44\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f5818705-7db4-444f-92c9-0b7947843f35\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which set reproduces the forms of liberty promised in the Preamble?\",\"hi\":\"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा समूह उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) में सुनिश्चित स्वतंत्रता के सभी रूपों को सही ढंग से प्रस्तुत करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Movement, residence, profession and property\",\"hi\":\"संचरण, निवास, व्यवसाय और संपत्ति\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Trade, occupation, association and assembly\",\"hi\":\"व्यापार, उपजीविका, संघ और सभा\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Thought, expression, belief, faith and worship\",\"hi\":\"विचार, अभिव्यक्ति, विश्वास, धर्म और उपासना\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Press, privacy, education and travel\",\"hi\":\"प्रेस, निजता, शिक्षा और यात्रा\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 14-21, 25, 37-39A, 42, 46 and 51A, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; learner-facing meanings of Justice, Liberty, Equality and Fraternity\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-240; individual freedom, social justice, equality, fraternity and common national identity\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Preamble, PDF p. 31 and Article 19(1)(a), PDF p. 39\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f53720e0-fe64-4294-a23a-3df2d00636d4\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 326 bases elections to the House of the People and State Legislative Assemblies on:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 326 लोक सभा और राज्य विधान सभाओं के चुनाव किस आधार पर रखता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Hereditary nomination\",\"hi\":\"वंशानुगत नामांकन\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Property ownership\",\"hi\":\"संपत्ति स्वामित्व\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Educational qualification alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल शैक्षिक योग्यता\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Adult suffrage\",\"hi\":\"वयस्क मताधिकार\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 326. NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 3, Election and Representation, 2026-27 reprint, printed pp. 67-68. Direct official documents: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf); NCERT Chapter 3, Election and Representation (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps203.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f4cb5a7b-a523-4f1e-860e-8b13dcae1d46\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which statement correctly describes the legal status of the Hindi text published under Article 394A?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 394A के अधीन प्रकाशित हिंदी पाठ की कानूनी स्थिति का सही वर्णन कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It is merely a private study aid\",\"hi\":\"यह केवल निजी अध्ययन-सहायिका है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It is advisory only for State Governments\",\"hi\":\"यह केवल राज्य सरकारों के लिए परामर्शात्मक है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It is deemed the authoritative Hindi text for all purposes\",\"hi\":\"इसे सभी प्रयोजनों के लिए प्राधिकृत हिंदी पाठ माना जाता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It applies only to the Preamble\",\"hi\":\"यह केवल प्रस्तावना पर लागू होता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Article 394A(1)-(3) (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f383f3a0-267c-4135-ae55-b141a7187ecc\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which Schedule demonstrates that the written Constitution contains three legislative lists?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सी अनुसूची दर्शाती है कि लिखित संविधान में तीन विधायी सूचियाँ हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Third Schedule\",\"hi\":\"तीसरी अनुसूची\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Seventh Schedule\",\"hi\":\"सातवीं अनुसूची\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Eighth Schedule\",\"hi\":\"आठवीं अनुसूची\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Tenth Schedule\",\"hi\":\"दसवीं अनुसूची\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Article 246 and Seventh Schedule—Union, State and Concurrent Lists (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f36b36de-f047-47ca-8776-8eb81c85ae32\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What is the basic-structure consequence of recognising rule of law as a basic feature?\",\"hi\":\"विधि के शासन को मूल विशेषता मानने का मूल-संरचना संबंधी परिणाम क्या है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Every ordinary law is valid even if unconstitutional\",\"hi\":\"हर साधारण कानून असंवैधानिक होने पर भी वैध है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Parliament cannot use Article 368 to destroy the Constitution’s rule-of-law foundation\",\"hi\":\"संसद अनुच्छेद 368 से संविधान के विधि-शासन आधार को नष्ट नहीं कर सकती\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Courts may never examine constitutional amendments\",\"hi\":\"न्यायालय कभी संविधान संशोधन नहीं जाँच सकते\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The executive may suspend all legal limits permanently\",\"hi\":\"कार्यपालिका सभी विधिक सीमाएँ स्थायी रूप से निलंबित कर सकती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Supreme Court of India, In Re: Directions in the matter of demolition of structures, 2024 INSC 866, judgment dated 13 November 2024, paragraph 22, official PDF pp. 32-33; Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 368. Direct official documents: Supreme Court of India, In Re: Directions in the matter of demolition of structures, 2024 INSC 866 (official PDF: https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2022/12239/12239_2022_2_1501_57147_Judgement_13-Nov-2024.pdf); Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f30a8b7d-12e4-43ea-bd74-ed65a3c1b76f\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which Article guarantees the right to move the Supreme Court for enforcement of Fundamental Rights?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सा अनुच्छेद मौलिक अधिकारों के प्रवर्तन के लिए सर्वोच्च न्यायालय जाने के अधिकार की गारंटी देता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Article 21\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 21\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 32\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 32\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 136\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 136\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 226\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 226\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 32(1)-(2). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f2c615c7-7ce9-4841-8ff9-3a80d556d385\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which statement correctly describes the role of an affected State Legislature under the proviso to Article 3?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 3 के परंतुक के अधीन प्रभावित राज्य विधानमंडल की भूमिका का सही वर्णन कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Its unanimous consent is constitutionally mandatory\",\"hi\":\"उसकी सर्वसम्मत सहमति संवैधानिक रूप से अनिवार्य है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The President refers the Bill for its views within a specified period; its consent is not made binding\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति विधेयक को निर्धारित अवधि में उसके विचारों के लिए भेजते हैं; उसकी सहमति को बाध्यकारी नहीं बनाया गया है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It may itself amend the First Schedule\",\"hi\":\"वह स्वयं पहली अनुसूची में संशोधन कर सकता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It decides the Bill by referendum\",\"hi\":\"वह जनमत-संग्रह से विधेयक तय करता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), proviso to Article 3, PDF p. 33; Supreme Court of India, In Re: Article 370 of the Constitution, judgment dated 11 December 2023, paragraphs 510-511, PDF pp. 344-346. Direct official documents: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf); Supreme Court of India, In Re: Article 370, judgment dated 11 December 2023 (official PDF: https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2019/29796/29796_2019_1_1501_49019_Judgement_11-Dec-2023.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f234adbb-bebb-48f2-95a3-330a2efc5e2a\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 75(1B) bars which person from being appointed a Union Minister for the constitutionally specified period?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 75(1B) संवैधानिक रूप से निर्दिष्ट अवधि तक किस व्यक्ति को संघीय मंत्री नियुक्त होने से रोकता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Every defeated election candidate\",\"hi\":\"हर पराजित चुनाव प्रत्याशी\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Every former civil servant\",\"hi\":\"हर पूर्व लोक सेवक\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A member disqualified under paragraph 2 of the Tenth Schedule\",\"hi\":\"दसवीं अनुसूची के पैरा 2 के अधीन अयोग्य घोषित सदस्य\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Every member of Rajya Sabha\",\"hi\":\"राज्यसभा का हर सदस्य\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 75(1B) and Tenth Schedule, paragraph 2, PDF pp. 65 and 375-376. Direct official document: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f17fadea-3a26-4ebe-ab25-747e2cf77e20\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Under Article 161, the Governor’s clemency power extends to offences against laws relating to matters within:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 161 के अधीन राज्यपाल की दया शक्ति उन कानूनों के विरुद्ध अपराधों तक फैली है जो किन विषयों से संबंधित हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Only the Union executive power\",\"hi\":\"केवल संघ की कार्यपालिका शक्ति\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The Supreme Court’s advisory jurisdiction\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय की परामर्शी अधिकारिता\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The executive power of the State\",\"hi\":\"राज्य की कार्यपालिका शक्ति\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The privileges of Parliament alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल संसद के विशेषाधिकार\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 161. Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f171bb4b-6a52-44b9-ab02-4409e2c816d1\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which Directive Principle most directly requires the State to promote welfare through a social order informed by social, economic and political justice?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सा नीति-निदेशक तत्व राज्य को सामाजिक, आर्थिक और राजनीतिक न्याय से अनुप्राणित सामाजिक व्यवस्था द्वारा लोक-कल्याण बढ़ाने का सबसे सीधा निर्देश देता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Article 25\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 25\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 325\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 325\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 253\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 253\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 38\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 38\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 13-16, 19(1)(g), 25-30, 38-43, 47, 51, 51A(e), 253 and 325, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Sovereign, Socialist and Secular on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; constitutional philosophy, individual freedom, social justice, secularism and national identity\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Article 38(1)-(2), PDF p. 51\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f1152a60-eeab-4827-9525-ac625c88d7f9\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Under Article 88, a Minister who is not a member of a particular House may:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 88 के अधीन किसी विशेष सदन का सदस्य न होने वाला मंत्री क्या कर सकता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Vote there solely because of ministerial office\",\"hi\":\"केवल मंत्री-पद के कारण वहाँ मतदान कर सकता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Preside permanently over that House\",\"hi\":\"उस सदन की स्थायी अध्यक्षता कर सकता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Dissolve that House personally\",\"hi\":\"व्यक्तिगत रूप से उस सदन को भंग कर सकता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Speak and take part in its proceedings but not vote there merely by virtue of Article 88\",\"hi\":\"उसकी कार्यवाही में बोल और भाग ले सकता है, पर केवल अनुच्छेद 88 के आधार पर वहाँ मतदान नहीं कर सकता\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 88, PDF p. 71. Direct official document: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f0eb8c54-b4f2-4722-97cd-fcbf5c874ba9\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Why does NCERT describe the Indian Constitution as a living document?\",\"hi\":\"NCERT भारतीय संविधान को जीवंत दस्तावेज क्यों बताता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It cannot be amended\",\"hi\":\"इसमें संशोधन नहीं हो सकता\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It balances continuity with the capacity for constitutional change\",\"hi\":\"यह निरंतरता और संवैधानिक परिवर्तन की क्षमता में संतुलन रखता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It is replaced after every election\",\"hi\":\"इसे प्रत्येक चुनाव के बाद बदल दिया जाता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It contains only conventions\",\"hi\":\"इसमें केवल परंपराएँ हैं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 9, printed pp. 198-200 (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps209.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f05a9fd6-51cb-4ef0-9ac5-3c31d34856ca\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Equality of opportunity in matters of public employment or appointment under the State is expressly stated in:\",\"hi\":\"राज्य के अधीन किसी पद पर नियोजन या नियुक्ति के विषय में अवसर की समानता का स्पष्ट प्रावधान किस अनुच्छेद में है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Article 14 alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल अनुच्छेद 14\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 15(2)\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 15(2)\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 18(1)\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 18(1)\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 16(1)\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 16(1)\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 14-21, 25, 37-39A, 42, 46 and 51A, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; learner-facing meanings of Justice, Liberty, Equality and Fraternity\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-240; individual freedom, social justice, equality, fraternity and common national identity\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Article 16(1)-(4), PDF p. 38\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f057a9cf-1112-4f1e-9e7f-a46f32edad94\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"How does an integrated judiciary differ from a dual judicial system?\",\"hi\":\"एकीकृत न्यायपालिका दोहरी न्यायिक व्यवस्था से कैसे भिन्न होती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It abolishes all State-level courts\",\"hi\":\"यह राज्य स्तर के सभी न्यायालय समाप्त कर देती है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It links Union and State-level courts in one hierarchy instead of maintaining wholly separate federal and State court systems\",\"hi\":\"यह पूर्णतः अलग संघीय और राज्य न्यायालय प्रणालियों के बजाय संघ और राज्य स्तर के न्यायालयों को एक पदानुक्रम में जोड़ती है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It prevents every court from applying Central laws\",\"hi\":\"यह प्रत्येक न्यायालय को केंद्रीय कानून लागू करने से रोकती है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It removes appellate review from the judiciary\",\"hi\":\"यह न्यायपालिका से अपीलीय समीक्षा हटा देती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Articles 132-136 and 141. NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 6, Judiciary, 2026-27 reprint, printed pp. 131-134, integrated hierarchy and appellate jurisdiction. Direct official documents: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf); NCERT Class 11, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 6 Judiciary (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps206.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f030dc24-bf18-4dee-96c3-040dd931d8f3\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which set correctly states the five expressions used in the Preamble to describe the constitutional character of India?\",\"hi\":\"भारत के संवैधानिक स्वरूप का वर्णन करने के लिए उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) में प्रयुक्त पाँच अभिव्यक्तियों का सही समूह कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Sovereign, Socialist, Secular, Democratic, Republic\",\"hi\":\"संपूर्ण प्रभुत्व-संपन्न, समाजवादी, पंथनिरपेक्ष, लोकतंत्रात्मक, गणराज्य\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Federal, Socialist, Secular, Parliamentary, Republic\",\"hi\":\"संघीय, समाजवादी, पंथनिरपेक्ष, संसदीय, गणराज्य\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Sovereign, Liberal, Secular, Presidential, Republic\",\"hi\":\"संपूर्ण प्रभुत्व-संपन्न, उदारवादी, पंथनिरपेक्ष, अध्यक्षात्मक, गणराज्य\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Unitary, Socialist, Religious, Democratic, Monarchy\",\"hi\":\"एकात्मक, समाजवादी, धार्मिक, लोकतंत्रात्मक, राजतंत्र\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified with: Constitution, Preamble, printed p. 31; Evidence locator: Preamble, printed page 31; Direct clickable source(s): The Constitution of India, diglot edition: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf; Confidence: high; Originality: independently written; no PYQ, textbook exercise, coaching question, or copyrighted explanation has been copied.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India, diglot edition\",\"institution\":\"Government of India, Legislative Department\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Preamble, printed page 31\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ee87f1a0-8d12-4fd6-8913-9f2978244d13\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"At the State level, the Council of Ministers is collectively responsible to the:\",\"hi\":\"राज्य स्तर पर मंत्रिपरिषद सामूहिक रूप से किसके प्रति उत्तरदायी है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Legislative Council alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल विधान परिषद\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Legislative Assembly of the State\",\"hi\":\"राज्य की विधान सभा\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Governor personally\",\"hi\":\"व्यक्तिगत रूप से राज्यपाल\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"High Court\",\"hi\":\"उच्च न्यायालय\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 164(2), PDF p. 103. Direct official document: Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ee533992-2187-4401-9f41-39de20192911\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"At the Union level, collective responsibility of the Council of Ministers is constitutionally owed to:\",\"hi\":\"संघ स्तर पर मंत्रिपरिषद की सामूहिक उत्तरदायित्व संवैधानिक रूप से किसके प्रति है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The Supreme Court\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The Council of States alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल राज्यों की परिषद्\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The Election Commission\",\"hi\":\"निर्वाचन आयोग\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The House of the People\",\"hi\":\"लोक सभा\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 75(3). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ecc88056-5610-421e-9cba-c780affb886a\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"In the expression “Democratic Republic”, what does “Republic” primarily signify?\",\"hi\":\"“लोकतांत्रिक गणराज्य” पदबंध में “गणराज्य” शब्द मुख्यतः किस संवैधानिक विशेषता को व्यक्त करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The head of State is not a hereditary ruler\",\"hi\":\"राज्याध्यक्ष वंशानुगत शासक नहीं होता\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Every public employee is directly elected\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक लोक कर्मचारी प्रत्यक्ष निर्वाचित होता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The legislature can never be dissolved\",\"hi\":\"विधानमंडल कभी विघटित नहीं हो सकता\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The judiciary is chosen by universal voting\",\"hi\":\"न्यायपालिका सार्वभौम मतदान से चुनी जाती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 52, 54-58, 61-62, 75(3), 79, 81, 83, 324-326, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Democratic and Republic on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; popular participation, universal franchise and constitutional philosophy\"},{\"title\":\"Senior Secondary Political Science (317), Lesson 5: Preamble and Salient Features\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS)\",\"url\":\"https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/317en/317EL5.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Lesson 5, section 5.5, Democratic Republic, printed p. 49\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"NIOS Political Science (317), Lesson 5, section 5.5, printed p. 49; Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Articles 52 and 54\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ec48a0c0-4b62-4446-84fe-8b17aef4b855\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"How many Schedules are listed in the official Constitution edition updated through the 106th Amendment?\",\"hi\":\"106वें संशोधन तक अद्यतन आधिकारिक संविधान संस्करण में कितनी अनुसूचियाँ सूचीबद्ध हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Twelve\",\"hi\":\"बारह\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Eight\",\"hi\":\"आठ\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Ten\",\"hi\":\"दस\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Twenty-two\",\"hi\":\"बाईस\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Preface and Contents—First through Twelfth Schedules (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ebf79762-eb3d-42a8-b8f5-310f3558a9b7\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which statement correctly distinguishes the Preamble from Fundamental Rights?\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) और मौलिक अधिकारों के बीच सही अंतर कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The Preamble overrides clear Article wording whenever a broad constitutional value points in another direction\",\"hi\":\"जब कोई व्यापक संवैधानिक मूल्य दूसरी दिशा इंगित करे, तब उद्देशिका स्पष्ट अनुच्छेद-भाषा को अधिलिखित कर देती है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The Preamble and every Fundamental Right are independently enforceable in exactly the same manner\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका और प्रत्येक मौलिक अधिकार बिल्कुल समान रूप से स्वतंत्रतः प्रवर्तनीय हैं\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Fundamental Rights merely restate political aspirations and have no operative legal effect\",\"hi\":\"मौलिक अधिकार केवल राजनीतिक आकांक्षाओं को दोहराते हैं और उनका कोई क्रियात्मक विधिक प्रभाव नहीं है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The Preamble states foundational goals, while enforceable Fundamental Rights are contained in operative constitutional provisions\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका आधारभूत लक्ष्य व्यक्त करती है, जबकि प्रवर्तनीय मौलिक अधिकार संविधान के क्रियात्मक प्रावधानों में निहित हैं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"Constitution Articles 13, 32 and 226; Kesavananda Bharati para 1526\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (diglot, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Government of India, Legislative Department\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Kesavananda Bharati Sripadagalvaru v. State of Kerala\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/29981.pdf\",\"citation\":\"(1973) 4 SCC 225\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Articles 13 printed p.36, 32 printed p.49, 226 printed p.134; Kesavananda para 1526, PDF p.345\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ebf001be-199c-428d-83f8-d264b35ea4d9\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 20(3) protects an accused person from being compelled to:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 20(3) किसी अभियुक्त व्यक्ति को किसके लिए विवश किए जाने से बचाता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Appear before any lawful court\",\"hi\":\"किसी वैध न्यायालय में उपस्थित होने\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Be a witness against himself or herself\",\"hi\":\"अपने ही विरुद्ध साक्षी बनने\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Provide every form of physical evidence\",\"hi\":\"हर प्रकार का भौतिक साक्ष्य देने\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Face a lawfully framed charge\",\"hi\":\"वैध रूप से बनाए आरोप का सामना करने\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 20(3). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ea83c300-2780-4eb8-bb41-d74fc09e0ac9\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which group is excluded from the Presidential electoral college described in Article 54?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 54 में निर्धारित राष्ट्रपति के निर्वाचक मंडल में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा समूह सम्मिलित नहीं है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Elected members of the Lok Sabha\",\"hi\":\"लोकसभा के निर्वाचित सदस्य\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Nominated members of Parliament\",\"hi\":\"संसद के मनोनीत सदस्य\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Elected members of State Legislative Assemblies\",\"hi\":\"राज्य विधानसभाओं के निर्वाचित सदस्य\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Elected members of the Rajya Sabha\",\"hi\":\"राज्यसभा के निर्वाचित सदस्य\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department,